# Recursion at a different compile-time argument every time, which compiles a
# new copy forever and must be stopped with an explanation rather than by
# running out of memory.
#
# This case pins two things `spec/inference-rewrite.md` phase 6 changed. The
# depth guard used to be the C++ call stack's own depth, because instance
# bodies were checked by recursive calls; now bodies are checked from a
# worklist, and each pending instance carries the depth it was requested at.
# And the "instantiated from here" chain used to be read off a live stack that
# a deferred body no longer has, so it is captured whole at request time.
# Nothing else in the suite exercises either, and getting the first wrong
# means the compiler hangs instead of teaching.
module infer_diag.instantiation_depth

def climb[n: usize]() -> unit:
    climb[n + 1]()

def wrong() -> unit:
    climb[0]()
